Two fixes, and the gesture should now actually work.

The microphone was taking the headset anyway when tap-to-talk was on, because
the check that defers it tested something not yet true at connect time.

And taps were being detected and then thrown away: the switch that lets a
gesture act was set before the engine existed, so the call failed silently and
the flag stayed off for the whole session.

If a tap still does nothing, please read out the Motion rows in Diagnostics.
